      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Getting Started with CloudScale Stream API\n=============================================\n\nTo begin using the CloudScale Stream API, follow these steps:\n\nTo start using the CloudScale Stream API, you'll need an API key. You can obtain a key by creating a new account on the CloudScale website or revoking and re-issuing a key from your existing account. Once you have your API key, you can use it to make authenticated requests to the Stream API. \n\nTo make your first authenticated request, begin by initializing the `client` object with your API key. This object will handle all of the authentication and request logic on your behalf. You can use a library such as `axios` or `curl` to make HTTP requests to the Stream API using the `client` object. \n\nHere's an example of how to make an authenticated GET request to retrieve a list of streams: \n```javascript\nconst apiEndpoint = 'https://api.cloudscale.io/v1';\nconst apiKey = 'YOUR_API_KEY';\nconst client = new ApiClient(apiKey);\n\nconst response = await client.getStreamList();\nconsole.log(response.data);\n```\nThis is just a starting point, and you'll likely need to adapt this example to fit your specific use case. However",
      "source": "target",
